NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI provides a complete realtime voice chat system for building voice-to-voice AI interactions. The realtime API supports multiple providers (OpenAI, ElevenLabs), automatic tool execution, audio visualization, and multimodal input including images."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime voice chat differs from text-based chat in several key ways:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bidirectional audio"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Users speak into a microphone, and the AI responds with synthesized voice"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice Activity Detection (VAD)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Automatically detects when the user starts and stops speaking"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interruptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Users can interrupt the AI mid-response"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Low latency"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Uses WebRTC or WebSocket connections for near-instant communication"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multimodal"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Supports text input, image input, and tool calling alongside voice"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The realtime system follows the same adapter architecture as the rest of TanStack AI:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server"}]},{"type":"text","value":" generates ephemeral tokens using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"realtimeToken()"},{"type":"text","value":" with a provider-specific token adapter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"text","value":" connects using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RealtimeClient"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRealtimeChat"},{"type":"text","value":" in React) with a provider-specific connection adapter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" handle the protocol differences between OpenAI WebRTC, ElevenLabs WebSocket, etc."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-set-up-the-server-token-endpoint","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Set Up the Server Token Endpoint"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server generates short-lived tokens so your API keys never reach the client:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst getRealtimeToken = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .handler(async () => {\n    return realtimeToken({\n      adapter: openaiRealtimeToken({\n        model: 'gpt-realtime-2.1',\n      }),\n    })\n  })","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"realtimeToken()"},{"type":"text","value":" function works with any server framework. The example above uses TanStack Start, but you can use Express, Hono, Fastify, or any other framework that can handle HTTP requests."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-connect-from-the-client-react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Connect from the Client (React)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nfunction VoiceChat() {\n  const {\n    status,\n    mode,\n    messages,\n    connect,\n    disconnect,\n    pendingUserTranscript,\n    pendingAssistantTranscript,\n    inputLevel,\n    outputLevel,\n  } = useRealtimeChat({\n    getToken: () => fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then(r => r.json()),\n    adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n    instructions: 'You are a helpful voice assistant.',\n    voice: 'alloy',\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Status: {status}</p>\n      <p>Mode: {mode}</p>\n      <button onClick={status === 'idle' ? connect : disconnect}>\n        {status === 'idle' ? 'Start Conversation' : 'End Conversation'}\n      </button>\n      {pendingUserTranscript && <p>You: {pendingUserTranscript}...</p>}\n      {pendingAssistantTranscript && <p>AI: {pendingAssistantTranscript}...</p>}\n      {messages.map((msg) => (\n        <div key={msg.id}>\n          <strong>{msg.role}:</strong>\n          {msg.parts.map((part, i) => (\n            <span key={i}>\n              {part.type === 'text' ? part.content : null}\n              {part.type === 'audio' ? part.transcript : null}\n            </span>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"openai-realtime","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI Realtime"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI's realtime API uses WebRTC for low-latency voice communication."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server (token generation):"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: openaiRealtimeToken({\n    model: 'gpt-realtime-2.1',\n  }),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client (connection):"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst adapter = openaiRealtime()","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment variables:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available models:"}]}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-realtime-2.1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latest full realtime model (default)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-realtime-2.1-mini"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latest smaller, faster realtime model"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-realtime-2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Previous full realtime model"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-realtime-1.5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Earlier full realtime model"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-realtime"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Original full realtime model"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gpt-realtime-mini"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Original smaller, faster realtime model"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available voices:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"alloy"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ash"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ballad"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"coral"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"echo"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sage"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shimmer"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"verse"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"marin"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cedar"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"elevenlabs-realtime","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs Realtime"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs uses WebSocket connections and requires an agent configured in their dashboard."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server (token generation):"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n    agentId: 'your-agent-id',\n  }),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client (connection):"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst adapter = elevenlabsRealtime()","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment variables:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ELEVENLABS_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID"},{"type":"text","value":" (optional)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"voice-activity-detection-vad","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice Activity Detection (VAD)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"VAD controls when the system detects that you've started and stopped speaking. Three modes are available:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How it works"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best for"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The provider detects speech server-side using audio energy levels"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default — simple, low client complexity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"semantic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Detects end-of-utterance using semantic cues like pauses and sentence completion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Natural conversation — avoids cutting you off mid-sentence"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manual"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startListening()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stopListening()"},{"type":"text","value":" explicitly"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Push-to-talk interfaces"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set the VAD mode when creating the hook:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { startListening, stopListening, updateSession } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  vadMode: 'manual', // or 'server' or 'semantic'\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manual"},{"type":"text","value":" VAD mode, use push-to-talk style interactions:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<button onMouseDown={startListening} onMouseUp={stopListening}>\n  Hold to talk\n</button>","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can switch VAD mode at runtime without reconnecting, via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updateSession"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"updateSession({ vadMode: 'semantic' })","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For semantic VAD, configure eagerness to control how long the model waits before deciding you've finished speaking:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  vadMode: 'semantic',\n  semanticEagerness: 'low', // waits longer before detecting end-of-speech\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime sessions support client-side tools. Define tools using the standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition()"},{"type":"text","value":" API and pass their client implementations:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Get weather for a location',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string().meta({ description: 'City name' }),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    conditions: z.string(),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.client(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/weather?location=${location}`)\n  return res.json()\n})\n\n// Pass tools to the hook\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The realtime client automatically executes tool calls and sends results back to the provider. Tool calls appear as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-call"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-result"},{"type":"text","value":" parts in messages."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-and-image-input","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text and Image Input"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In addition to voice, you can send text messages and images:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { base64ImageData } from './assets'\n\nconst { sendText, sendImage } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Send a text message\nsendText('What is the weather like today?')\n\n// Send an image (base64 data or URL)\nsendImage(base64ImageData, 'image/png')","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"audio-visualization","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio Visualization"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRealtimeChat"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes audio analysis data for building level meters, waveforms, and spectrum analyzers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst {\n  inputLevel,    // 0–1 normalized microphone level\n  outputLevel,   // 0–1 normalized speaker level\n  getInputFrequencyData,   // Uint8Array — FFT bins for spectrum analyzer\n  getOutputFrequencyData,\n  getInputTimeDomainData,  // Uint8Array — waveform samples for oscilloscope\n  getOutputTimeDomainData,\n} = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputLevel"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputLevel"},{"type":"text","value":" values update on every animation frame while connected, making them suitable for driving CSS animations or canvas visualizations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Simple level meter:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div style={{ width: `${inputLevel * 100}%`, height: 4, background: 'green' }} />","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pulsing audio indicator:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function AudioIndicator({ level }: { level: number }) {\n  return (\n    <div\n      style={{\n        width: 40,\n        height: 40,\n        borderRadius: '50%',\n        transform: `scale(${1 + level * 0.5})`,\n        backgroundColor: `rgba(59, 130, 246, ${0.3 + level * 0.7})`,\n        transition: 'transform 0.1s ease',\n      }}\n    />\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spectrum analyzer using canvas:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function drawSpectrum(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement) {\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')!\n  const draw = () => {\n    const data = getInputFrequencyData()\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height)\n    const barWidth = canvas.width / data.length\n    data.forEach((value, i) => {\n      const height = (value / 255) * canvas.height\n      ctx.fillRect(i * barWidth, canvas.height - height, barWidth - 1, height)\n    })\n    requestAnimationFrame(draw)\n  }\n  draw()\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"interruptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interruptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Users can interrupt the AI while it's speaking:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { interrupt, mode } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Programmatically interrupt\nif (mode === 'speaking') {\n  interrupt()\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With server or semantic VAD, interruptions happen automatically when the user starts speaking. Interrupted messages are marked with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupted: true"},{"type":"text","value":" in the messages array."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"using-realtimeclient-directly","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using RealtimeClient Directly"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For non-React applications or more control, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RealtimeClient"},{"type":"text","value":" directly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { RealtimeClient } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst client = new RealtimeClient({\n  getToken: () => fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then(r => r.json()),\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  instructions: 'You are a helpful assistant.',\n  voice: 'alloy',\n  onMessage: (message) => {\n    console.log(`${message.role}:`, message.parts)\n  },\n  onStatusChange: (status) => {\n    console.log('Status:', status)\n  },\n  onModeChange: (mode) => {\n    console.log('Mode:', mode)\n  },\n})\n\n// Connect\nawait client.connect()\n\n// Send text\nclient.sendText('Hello!')\n\n// Subscribe to state changes\nconst unsub = client.onStateChange((state) => {\n  console.log('Messages:', state.messages.length)\n})\n\n// Disconnect when done\nawait client.disconnect()\n\n// Clean up\nclient.destroy()","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"using-elevenlabs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using ElevenLabs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI supports "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/elevenlabs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" as an alternative realtime voice provider. The client API is identical — swap the adapter and token function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst { status, messages, connect, disconnect } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () => fetch('/api/elevenlabs-token').then(r => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ElevenLabs uses agent-based configuration — voice and system prompt are set in the ElevenLabs dashboard or via token overrides. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/elevenlabs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs adapter page"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for setup details."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about the isomorphic tool system"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./text-to-speech","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text-to-Speech"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Non-realtime speech generation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/multimodal-content","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multimodal Content"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Working with images, audio, and video"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/elevenlabs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ElevenLabs Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - ElevenLabs realtime voice provider setup and configuration"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"advanced","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reference detail you do not need to get this working."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"session-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Session Configuration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure the realtime session through the hook options:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getToken"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => Promise<RealtimeToken>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function to fetch a token from the server"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RealtimeAdapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider adapter ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiRealtime()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsRealtime()"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"System instructions for the assistant"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"voice"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice to use for audio output"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyClientTool[]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-side tools with execution logic"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vadMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'server' | 'semantic' | 'manual'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'server'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voice activity detection mode"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"semanticEagerness"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'low' | 'medium' | 'high'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eagerness for semantic VAD"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"autoPlayback"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Auto-play assistant audio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"autoCapture"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Request microphone on connect"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputModalities"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<'audio' | 'text'>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Response modalities"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation temperature"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxOutputTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | 'inf'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"—"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Max tokens in a response"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"connection-lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connection Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The realtime client manages a connection lifecycle with these statuses:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Status"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not connected"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connecting"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Establishing connection"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connected"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Active session"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconnecting"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reconnecting after interruption"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connection error occurred"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And these modes while connected:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connected but not actively interacting"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listening"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capturing user audio input"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thinking"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Processing user input"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"speaking"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AI is generating a response"}]}]]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { useEffect } from 'react'\n\nconst { status, mode, error, connect, disconnect } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Handle connection\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (status === 'error' && error) {\n    console.error('Connection error:', error.message)\n  }\n}, [status, error])","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"message-structure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Message Structure"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Realtime messages use a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parts"},{"type":"text","value":"-based structure similar to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIMessage"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { RealtimeMessagePart } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\ninterface RealtimeMessage {\n  id: string\n  role: 'user' | 'assistant'\n  timestamp: number\n  parts: Array<RealtimeMessagePart>\n  interrupted?: boolean\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each part can be one of:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Part Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fields"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text content from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendText()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"audio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transcript"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"durationMs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transcribed voice content"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"arguments"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"output"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool invocation"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCallId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool execution result"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"image"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mimeType"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Image sent via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendImage()"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"error-handling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle errors through the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":" callback or the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" state:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { error } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  onError: (err: Error) => {\n    if (err.message.includes('Permission denied')) {\n      alert('Microphone access is required for voice chat.')\n    } else {\n      console.error('Realtime error:', err)\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"best-practices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best Practices"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Token security"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Always generate tokens server-side. Never expose API keys to the client."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Microphone permissions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Handle the case where the user denies microphone access gracefully."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Always disconnect when unmounting components. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useRealtimeChat"},{"type":"text","value":" hook handles this automatically."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instructions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Keep voice assistant instructions concise. Remind the model it's in a voice interface so responses stay conversational."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool design"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Keep tool descriptions clear and tool outputs small, since results are processed in real time."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error recovery"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Implement retry logic for transient connection failures."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick Start","level":2},{"id":"1-set-up-the-server-token-endpoint","text":"1. Set Up the Server Token Endpoint","level":3},{"id":"2-connect-from-the-client-react","text":"2. Connect from the Client (React)","level":3},{"id":"providers","text":"Providers","level":2},{"id":"openai-realtime","text":"OpenAI Realtime","level":3},{"id":"elevenlabs-realtime","text":"ElevenLabs Realtime","level":3},{"id":"voice-activity-detection-vad","text":"Voice Activity Detection (VAD)","level":2},{"id":"tools","text":"Tools","level":2},{"id":"text-and-image-input","text":"Text and Image Input","level":2},{"id":"audio-visualization","text":"Audio Visualization","level":2},{"id":"interruptions","text":"Interruptions","level":2},{"id":"using-realtimeclient-directly","text":"Using RealtimeClient Directly","level":2},{"id":"using-elevenlabs","text":"Using ElevenLabs","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2},{"id":"advanced","text":"Advanced","level":2},{"id":"session-configuration","text":"Session Configuration","level":3},{"id":"connection-lifecycle","text":"Connection Lifecycle","level":3},{"id":"message-structure","text":"Message Structure","level":3},{"id":"error-handling","text":"Error Handling","level":3},{"id":"best-practices","text":"Best Practices","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack AI provides a complete realtime voice chat system for building voice-to-voice AI interactions. The realtime API supports multiple providers (OpenAI, ElevenLabs), automatic tool execution, audio visualization, and multimodal input including images.\n\n## Overview\n\nRealtime voice chat differs from text-based chat in several key ways:\n\n- **Bidirectional audio** - Users speak into a microphone, and the AI responds with synthesized voice\n- **Voice Activity Detection (VAD)** - Automatically detects when the user starts and stops speaking\n- **Interruptions** - Users can interrupt the AI mid-response\n- **Low latency** - Uses WebRTC or WebSocket connections for near-instant communication\n- **Multimodal** - Supports text input, image input, and tool calling alongside voice\n\nThe realtime system follows the same adapter architecture as the rest of TanStack AI:\n\n1. **Server** generates ephemeral tokens using `realtimeToken()` with a provider-specific token adapter\n2. **Client** connects using `RealtimeClient` (or `useRealtimeChat` in React) with a provider-specific connection adapter\n3. **Provider adapters** handle the protocol differences between OpenAI WebRTC, ElevenLabs WebSocket, etc.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 1. Set Up the Server Token Endpoint\n\nThe server generates short-lived tokens so your API keys never reach the client:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst getRealtimeToken = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .handler(async () => {\n    return realtimeToken({\n      adapter: openaiRealtimeToken({\n        model: 'gpt-realtime-2.1',\n      }),\n    })\n  })\n```\n\n> **Note:** The `realtimeToken()` function works with any server framework. The example above uses TanStack Start, but you can use Express, Hono, Fastify, or any other framework that can handle HTTP requests.\n\n### 2. Connect from the Client (React)\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nfunction VoiceChat() {\n  const {\n    status,\n    mode,\n    messages,\n    connect,\n    disconnect,\n    pendingUserTranscript,\n    pendingAssistantTranscript,\n    inputLevel,\n    outputLevel,\n  } = useRealtimeChat({\n    getToken: () => fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then(r => r.json()),\n    adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n    instructions: 'You are a helpful voice assistant.',\n    voice: 'alloy',\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Status: {status}</p>\n      <p>Mode: {mode}</p>\n      <button onClick={status === 'idle' ? connect : disconnect}>\n        {status === 'idle' ? 'Start Conversation' : 'End Conversation'}\n      </button>\n      {pendingUserTranscript && <p>You: {pendingUserTranscript}...</p>}\n      {pendingAssistantTranscript && <p>AI: {pendingAssistantTranscript}...</p>}\n      {messages.map((msg) => (\n        <div key={msg.id}>\n          <strong>{msg.role}:</strong>\n          {msg.parts.map((part, i) => (\n            <span key={i}>\n              {part.type === 'text' ? part.content : null}\n              {part.type === 'audio' ? part.transcript : null}\n            </span>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Providers\n\n### OpenAI Realtime\n\nOpenAI's realtime API uses WebRTC for low-latency voice communication.\n\n**Server (token generation):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: openaiRealtimeToken({\n    model: 'gpt-realtime-2.1',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n**Client (connection):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst adapter = openaiRealtime()\n```\n\n**Environment variables:** `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n\n**Available models:**\n\n| Model | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `gpt-realtime-2.1` | Latest full realtime model (default) |\n| `gpt-realtime-2.1-mini` | Latest smaller, faster realtime model |\n| `gpt-realtime-2` | Previous full realtime model |\n| `gpt-realtime-1.5` | Earlier full realtime model |\n| `gpt-realtime` | Original full realtime model |\n| `gpt-realtime-mini` | Original smaller, faster realtime model |\n\n**Available voices:** `alloy`, `ash`, `ballad`, `coral`, `echo`, `sage`, `shimmer`, `verse`, `marin`, `cedar`\n\n### ElevenLabs Realtime\n\nElevenLabs uses WebSocket connections and requires an agent configured in their dashboard.\n\n**Server (token generation):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n    agentId: 'your-agent-id',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n**Client (connection):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst adapter = elevenlabsRealtime()\n```\n\n**Environment variables:** `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`, `ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID` (optional)\n\n## Voice Activity Detection (VAD)\n\nVAD controls when the system detects that you've started and stopped speaking. Three modes are available:\n\n| Mode | How it works | Best for |\n|------|-------------|----------|\n| `server` | The provider detects speech server-side using audio energy levels | Default — simple, low client complexity |\n| `semantic` | Detects end-of-utterance using semantic cues like pauses and sentence completion | Natural conversation — avoids cutting you off mid-sentence |\n| `manual` | You call `startListening()` / `stopListening()` explicitly | Push-to-talk interfaces |\n\nSet the VAD mode when creating the hook:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { startListening, stopListening, updateSession } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  vadMode: 'manual', // or 'server' or 'semantic'\n})\n```\n\nWith `manual` VAD mode, use push-to-talk style interactions:\n\n```tsx ignore\n<button onMouseDown={startListening} onMouseUp={stopListening}>\n  Hold to talk\n</button>\n```\n\nYou can switch VAD mode at runtime without reconnecting, via `updateSession`:\n\n```typescript ignore\nupdateSession({ vadMode: 'semantic' })\n```\n\nFor semantic VAD, configure eagerness to control how long the model waits before deciding you've finished speaking:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  vadMode: 'semantic',\n  semanticEagerness: 'low', // waits longer before detecting end-of-speech\n})\n```\n\n## Tools\n\nRealtime sessions support client-side tools. Define tools using the standard `toolDefinition()` API and pass their client implementations:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Get weather for a location',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string().meta({ description: 'City name' }),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    conditions: z.string(),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.client(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/weather?location=${location}`)\n  return res.json()\n})\n\n// Pass tools to the hook\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n```\n\nThe realtime client automatically executes tool calls and sends results back to the provider. Tool calls appear as `tool-call` and `tool-result` parts in messages.\n\n## Text and Image Input\n\nIn addition to voice, you can send text messages and images:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { base64ImageData } from './assets'\n\nconst { sendText, sendImage } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Send a text message\nsendText('What is the weather like today?')\n\n// Send an image (base64 data or URL)\nsendImage(base64ImageData, 'image/png')\n```\n\n## Audio Visualization\n\n`useRealtimeChat` exposes audio analysis data for building level meters, waveforms, and spectrum analyzers.\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst {\n  inputLevel,    // 0–1 normalized microphone level\n  outputLevel,   // 0–1 normalized speaker level\n  getInputFrequencyData,   // Uint8Array — FFT bins for spectrum analyzer\n  getOutputFrequencyData,\n  getInputTimeDomainData,  // Uint8Array — waveform samples for oscilloscope\n  getOutputTimeDomainData,\n} = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n```\n\nThe `inputLevel` and `outputLevel` values update on every animation frame while connected, making them suitable for driving CSS animations or canvas visualizations.\n\n**Simple level meter:**\n\n```tsx ignore\n<div style={{ width: `${inputLevel * 100}%`, height: 4, background: 'green' }} />\n```\n\n**Pulsing audio indicator:**\n\n```tsx\nfunction AudioIndicator({ level }: { level: number }) {\n  return (\n    <div\n      style={{\n        width: 40,\n        height: 40,\n        borderRadius: '50%',\n        transform: `scale(${1 + level * 0.5})`,\n        backgroundColor: `rgba(59, 130, 246, ${0.3 + level * 0.7})`,\n        transition: 'transform 0.1s ease',\n      }}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n**Spectrum analyzer using canvas:**\n\n```typescript ignore\nfunction drawSpectrum(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement) {\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')!\n  const draw = () => {\n    const data = getInputFrequencyData()\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height)\n    const barWidth = canvas.width / data.length\n    data.forEach((value, i) => {\n      const height = (value / 255) * canvas.height\n      ctx.fillRect(i * barWidth, canvas.height - height, barWidth - 1, height)\n    })\n    requestAnimationFrame(draw)\n  }\n  draw()\n}\n```\n\n## Interruptions\n\nUsers can interrupt the AI while it's speaking:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { interrupt, mode } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Programmatically interrupt\nif (mode === 'speaking') {\n  interrupt()\n}\n```\n\nWith server or semantic VAD, interruptions happen automatically when the user starts speaking. Interrupted messages are marked with `interrupted: true` in the messages array.\n\n## Using RealtimeClient Directly\n\nFor non-React applications or more control, use `RealtimeClient` directly:\n\n```typescript\nimport { RealtimeClient } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst client = new RealtimeClient({\n  getToken: () => fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then(r => r.json()),\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  instructions: 'You are a helpful assistant.',\n  voice: 'alloy',\n  onMessage: (message) => {\n    console.log(`${message.role}:`, message.parts)\n  },\n  onStatusChange: (status) => {\n    console.log('Status:', status)\n  },\n  onModeChange: (mode) => {\n    console.log('Mode:', mode)\n  },\n})\n\n// Connect\nawait client.connect()\n\n// Send text\nclient.sendText('Hello!')\n\n// Subscribe to state changes\nconst unsub = client.onStateChange((state) => {\n  console.log('Messages:', state.messages.length)\n})\n\n// Disconnect when done\nawait client.disconnect()\n\n// Clean up\nclient.destroy()\n```\n\n## Using ElevenLabs\n\nTanStack AI supports [ElevenLabs](../adapters/elevenlabs) as an alternative realtime voice provider. The client API is identical — swap the adapter and token function:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst { status, messages, connect, disconnect } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () => fetch('/api/elevenlabs-token').then(r => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n})\n```\n\n> **Note:** ElevenLabs uses agent-based configuration — voice and system prompt are set in the ElevenLabs dashboard or via token overrides. See the [ElevenLabs adapter page](../adapters/elevenlabs) for setup details.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Tools](../tools/tools) - Learn about the isomorphic tool system\n- [Text-to-Speech](./text-to-speech) - Non-realtime speech generation\n- [Multimodal Content](../advanced/multimodal-content) - Working with images, audio, and video\n- [ElevenLabs Adapter](../adapters/elevenlabs) - ElevenLabs realtime voice provider setup and configuration\n\n## Advanced\n\nReference detail you do not need to get this working.\n\n### Session Configuration\n\nConfigure the realtime session through the hook options:\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `getToken` | `() => Promise<RealtimeToken>` | required | Function to fetch a token from the server |\n| `adapter` | `RealtimeAdapter` | required | Provider adapter (`openaiRealtime()`, `elevenlabsRealtime()`) |\n| `instructions` | `string` | — | System instructions for the assistant |\n| `voice` | `string` | — | Voice to use for audio output |\n| `tools` | `AnyClientTool[]` | — | Client-side tools with execution logic |\n| `vadMode` | `'server' \\| 'semantic' \\| 'manual'` | `'server'` | Voice activity detection mode |\n| `semanticEagerness` | `'low' \\| 'medium' \\| 'high'` | — | Eagerness for semantic VAD |\n| `autoPlayback` | `boolean` | `true` | Auto-play assistant audio |\n| `autoCapture` | `boolean` | `true` | Request microphone on connect |\n| `outputModalities` | `Array<'audio' \\| 'text'>` | — | Response modalities |\n| `temperature` | `number` | — | Generation temperature |\n| `maxOutputTokens` | `number \\| 'inf'` | — | Max tokens in a response |\n\n### Connection Lifecycle\n\nThe realtime client manages a connection lifecycle with these statuses:\n\n| Status | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `idle` | Not connected |\n| `connecting` | Establishing connection |\n| `connected` | Active session |\n| `reconnecting` | Reconnecting after interruption |\n| `error` | Connection error occurred |\n\nAnd these modes while connected:\n\n| Mode | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `idle` | Connected but not actively interacting |\n| `listening` | Capturing user audio input |\n| `thinking` | Processing user input |\n| `speaking` | AI is generating a response |\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { useEffect } from 'react'\n\nconst { status, mode, error, connect, disconnect } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Handle connection\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (status === 'error' && error) {\n    console.error('Connection error:', error.message)\n  }\n}, [status, error])\n```\n\n### Message Structure\n\nRealtime messages use a `parts`-based structure similar to `UIMessage`:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { RealtimeMessagePart } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\ninterface RealtimeMessage {\n  id: string\n  role: 'user' | 'assistant'\n  timestamp: number\n  parts: Array<RealtimeMessagePart>\n  interrupted?: boolean\n}\n```\n\nEach part can be one of:\n\n| Part Type | Fields | Description |\n|-----------|--------|-------------|\n| `text` | `content` | Text content from `sendText()` |\n| `audio` | `transcript`, `durationMs` | Transcribed voice content |\n| `tool-call` | `id`, `name`, `arguments`, `input`, `output` | Tool invocation |\n| `tool-result` | `toolCallId`, `content` | Tool execution result |\n| `image` | `data`, `mimeType` | Image sent via `sendImage()` |\n\n### Error Handling\n\nHandle errors through the `onError` callback or the `error` state:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { error } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  onError: (err: Error) => {\n    if (err.message.includes('Permission denied')) {\n      alert('Microphone access is required for voice chat.')\n    } else {\n      console.error('Realtime error:', err)\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Best Practices\n\n1. **Token security** - Always generate tokens server-side. Never expose API keys to the client.\n2. **Microphone permissions** - Handle the case where the user denies microphone access gracefully.\n3. **Cleanup** - Always disconnect when unmounting components. The `useRealtimeChat` hook handles this automatically.\n4. **Instructions** - Keep voice assistant instructions concise. Remind the model it's in a voice interface so responses stay conversational.\n5. **Tool design** - Keep tool descriptions clear and tool outputs small, since results are processed in real time.\n6. **Error recovery** - Implement retry logic for transient connection failures.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Realtime Voice Chat\nid: realtime-chat\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Build realtime voice-to-voice AI chat with TanStack AI — WebRTC and WebSocket, voice activity detection, interruptions, and multimodal input.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - realtime voice\n  - voice chat\n  - webrtc\n  - websocket\n  - vad\n  - voice ai\n  - multimodal\n  - useRealtimeChat\n---\n\nTanStack AI provides a complete realtime voice chat system for building voice-to-voice AI interactions. The realtime API supports multiple providers (OpenAI, ElevenLabs), automatic tool execution, audio visualization, and multimodal input including images.\n\n## Overview\n\nRealtime voice chat differs from text-based chat in several key ways:\n\n- **Bidirectional audio** - Users speak into a microphone, and the AI responds with synthesized voice\n- **Voice Activity Detection (VAD)** - Automatically detects when the user starts and stops speaking\n- **Interruptions** - Users can interrupt the AI mid-response\n- **Low latency** - Uses WebRTC or WebSocket connections for near-instant communication\n- **Multimodal** - Supports text input, image input, and tool calling alongside voice\n\nThe realtime system follows the same adapter architecture as the rest of TanStack AI:\n\n1. **Server** generates ephemeral tokens using `realtimeToken()` with a provider-specific token adapter\n2. **Client** connects using `RealtimeClient` (or `useRealtimeChat` in React) with a provider-specific connection adapter\n3. **Provider adapters** handle the protocol differences between OpenAI WebRTC, ElevenLabs WebSocket, etc.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 1. Set Up the Server Token Endpoint\n\nThe server generates short-lived tokens so your API keys never reach the client:\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { createServerFn } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst getRealtimeToken = createServerFn({ method: 'POST' })\n  .handler(async () => {\n    return realtimeToken({\n      adapter: openaiRealtimeToken({\n        model: 'gpt-realtime-2.1',\n      }),\n    })\n  })\n```\n\n> **Note:** The `realtimeToken()` function works with any server framework. The example above uses TanStack Start, but you can use Express, Hono, Fastify, or any other framework that can handle HTTP requests.\n\n### 2. Connect from the Client (React)\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nfunction VoiceChat() {\n  const {\n    status,\n    mode,\n    messages,\n    connect,\n    disconnect,\n    pendingUserTranscript,\n    pendingAssistantTranscript,\n    inputLevel,\n    outputLevel,\n  } = useRealtimeChat({\n    getToken: () => fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then(r => r.json()),\n    adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n    instructions: 'You are a helpful voice assistant.',\n    voice: 'alloy',\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>Status: {status}</p>\n      <p>Mode: {mode}</p>\n      <button onClick={status === 'idle' ? connect : disconnect}>\n        {status === 'idle' ? 'Start Conversation' : 'End Conversation'}\n      </button>\n      {pendingUserTranscript && <p>You: {pendingUserTranscript}...</p>}\n      {pendingAssistantTranscript && <p>AI: {pendingAssistantTranscript}...</p>}\n      {messages.map((msg) => (\n        <div key={msg.id}>\n          <strong>{msg.role}:</strong>\n          {msg.parts.map((part, i) => (\n            <span key={i}>\n              {part.type === 'text' ? part.content : null}\n              {part.type === 'audio' ? part.transcript : null}\n            </span>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Providers\n\n### OpenAI Realtime\n\nOpenAI's realtime API uses WebRTC for low-latency voice communication.\n\n**Server (token generation):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: openaiRealtimeToken({\n    model: 'gpt-realtime-2.1',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n**Client (connection):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst adapter = openaiRealtime()\n```\n\n**Environment variables:** `OPENAI_API_KEY`\n\n**Available models:**\n\n| Model | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `gpt-realtime-2.1` | Latest full realtime model (default) |\n| `gpt-realtime-2.1-mini` | Latest smaller, faster realtime model |\n| `gpt-realtime-2` | Previous full realtime model |\n| `gpt-realtime-1.5` | Earlier full realtime model |\n| `gpt-realtime` | Original full realtime model |\n| `gpt-realtime-mini` | Original smaller, faster realtime model |\n\n**Available voices:** `alloy`, `ash`, `ballad`, `coral`, `echo`, `sage`, `shimmer`, `verse`, `marin`, `cedar`\n\n### ElevenLabs Realtime\n\nElevenLabs uses WebSocket connections and requires an agent configured in their dashboard.\n\n**Server (token generation):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { realtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtimeToken } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst token = await realtimeToken({\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtimeToken({\n    agentId: 'your-agent-id',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n**Client (connection):**\n\n```typescript\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst adapter = elevenlabsRealtime()\n```\n\n**Environment variables:** `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`, `ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID` (optional)\n\n## Voice Activity Detection (VAD)\n\nVAD controls when the system detects that you've started and stopped speaking. Three modes are available:\n\n| Mode | How it works | Best for |\n|------|-------------|----------|\n| `server` | The provider detects speech server-side using audio energy levels | Default — simple, low client complexity |\n| `semantic` | Detects end-of-utterance using semantic cues like pauses and sentence completion | Natural conversation — avoids cutting you off mid-sentence |\n| `manual` | You call `startListening()` / `stopListening()` explicitly | Push-to-talk interfaces |\n\nSet the VAD mode when creating the hook:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { startListening, stopListening, updateSession } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  vadMode: 'manual', // or 'server' or 'semantic'\n})\n```\n\nWith `manual` VAD mode, use push-to-talk style interactions:\n\n```tsx ignore\n<button onMouseDown={startListening} onMouseUp={stopListening}>\n  Hold to talk\n</button>\n```\n\nYou can switch VAD mode at runtime without reconnecting, via `updateSession`:\n\n```typescript ignore\nupdateSession({ vadMode: 'semantic' })\n```\n\nFor semantic VAD, configure eagerness to control how long the model waits before deciding you've finished speaking:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  vadMode: 'semantic',\n  semanticEagerness: 'low', // waits longer before detecting end-of-speech\n})\n```\n\n## Tools\n\nRealtime sessions support client-side tools. Define tools using the standard `toolDefinition()` API and pass their client implementations:\n\n```typescript\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeatherDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Get weather for a location',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string().meta({ description: 'City name' }),\n  }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({\n    temperature: z.number(),\n    conditions: z.string(),\n  }),\n})\n\nconst getWeather = getWeatherDef.client(async ({ location }) => {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/weather?location=${location}`)\n  return res.json()\n})\n\n// Pass tools to the hook\nconst chat = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n```\n\nThe realtime client automatically executes tool calls and sends results back to the provider. Tool calls appear as `tool-call` and `tool-result` parts in messages.\n\n## Text and Image Input\n\nIn addition to voice, you can send text messages and images:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { base64ImageData } from './assets'\n\nconst { sendText, sendImage } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Send a text message\nsendText('What is the weather like today?')\n\n// Send an image (base64 data or URL)\nsendImage(base64ImageData, 'image/png')\n```\n\n## Audio Visualization\n\n`useRealtimeChat` exposes audio analysis data for building level meters, waveforms, and spectrum analyzers.\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst {\n  inputLevel,    // 0–1 normalized microphone level\n  outputLevel,   // 0–1 normalized speaker level\n  getInputFrequencyData,   // Uint8Array — FFT bins for spectrum analyzer\n  getOutputFrequencyData,\n  getInputTimeDomainData,  // Uint8Array — waveform samples for oscilloscope\n  getOutputTimeDomainData,\n} = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n```\n\nThe `inputLevel` and `outputLevel` values update on every animation frame while connected, making them suitable for driving CSS animations or canvas visualizations.\n\n**Simple level meter:**\n\n```tsx ignore\n<div style={{ width: `${inputLevel * 100}%`, height: 4, background: 'green' }} />\n```\n\n**Pulsing audio indicator:**\n\n```tsx\nfunction AudioIndicator({ level }: { level: number }) {\n  return (\n    <div\n      style={{\n        width: 40,\n        height: 40,\n        borderRadius: '50%',\n        transform: `scale(${1 + level * 0.5})`,\n        backgroundColor: `rgba(59, 130, 246, ${0.3 + level * 0.7})`,\n        transition: 'transform 0.1s ease',\n      }}\n    />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n**Spectrum analyzer using canvas:**\n\n```typescript ignore\nfunction drawSpectrum(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement) {\n  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d')!\n  const draw = () => {\n    const data = getInputFrequencyData()\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height)\n    const barWidth = canvas.width / data.length\n    data.forEach((value, i) => {\n      const height = (value / 255) * canvas.height\n      ctx.fillRect(i * barWidth, canvas.height - height, barWidth - 1, height)\n    })\n    requestAnimationFrame(draw)\n  }\n  draw()\n}\n```\n\n## Interruptions\n\nUsers can interrupt the AI while it's speaking:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { interrupt, mode } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Programmatically interrupt\nif (mode === 'speaking') {\n  interrupt()\n}\n```\n\nWith server or semantic VAD, interruptions happen automatically when the user starts speaking. Interrupted messages are marked with `interrupted: true` in the messages array.\n\n## Using RealtimeClient Directly\n\nFor non-React applications or more control, use `RealtimeClient` directly:\n\n```typescript\nimport { RealtimeClient } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst client = new RealtimeClient({\n  getToken: () => fetch('/api/realtime-token', { method: 'POST' }).then(r => r.json()),\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  instructions: 'You are a helpful assistant.',\n  voice: 'alloy',\n  onMessage: (message) => {\n    console.log(`${message.role}:`, message.parts)\n  },\n  onStatusChange: (status) => {\n    console.log('Status:', status)\n  },\n  onModeChange: (mode) => {\n    console.log('Mode:', mode)\n  },\n})\n\n// Connect\nawait client.connect()\n\n// Send text\nclient.sendText('Hello!')\n\n// Subscribe to state changes\nconst unsub = client.onStateChange((state) => {\n  console.log('Messages:', state.messages.length)\n})\n\n// Disconnect when done\nawait client.disconnect()\n\n// Clean up\nclient.destroy()\n```\n\n## Using ElevenLabs\n\nTanStack AI supports [ElevenLabs](../adapters/elevenlabs) as an alternative realtime voice provider. The client API is identical — swap the adapter and token function:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { elevenlabsRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-elevenlabs'\n\nconst { status, messages, connect, disconnect } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken: () => fetch('/api/elevenlabs-token').then(r => r.json()),\n  adapter: elevenlabsRealtime(),\n})\n```\n\n> **Note:** ElevenLabs uses agent-based configuration — voice and system prompt are set in the ElevenLabs dashboard or via token overrides. See the [ElevenLabs adapter page](../adapters/elevenlabs) for setup details.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Tools](../tools/tools) - Learn about the isomorphic tool system\n- [Text-to-Speech](./text-to-speech) - Non-realtime speech generation\n- [Multimodal Content](../advanced/multimodal-content) - Working with images, audio, and video\n- [ElevenLabs Adapter](../adapters/elevenlabs) - ElevenLabs realtime voice provider setup and configuration\n\n## Advanced\n\nReference detail you do not need to get this working.\n\n### Session Configuration\n\nConfigure the realtime session through the hook options:\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `getToken` | `() => Promise<RealtimeToken>` | required | Function to fetch a token from the server |\n| `adapter` | `RealtimeAdapter` | required | Provider adapter (`openaiRealtime()`, `elevenlabsRealtime()`) |\n| `instructions` | `string` | — | System instructions for the assistant |\n| `voice` | `string` | — | Voice to use for audio output |\n| `tools` | `AnyClientTool[]` | — | Client-side tools with execution logic |\n| `vadMode` | `'server' \\| 'semantic' \\| 'manual'` | `'server'` | Voice activity detection mode |\n| `semanticEagerness` | `'low' \\| 'medium' \\| 'high'` | — | Eagerness for semantic VAD |\n| `autoPlayback` | `boolean` | `true` | Auto-play assistant audio |\n| `autoCapture` | `boolean` | `true` | Request microphone on connect |\n| `outputModalities` | `Array<'audio' \\| 'text'>` | — | Response modalities |\n| `temperature` | `number` | — | Generation temperature |\n| `maxOutputTokens` | `number \\| 'inf'` | — | Max tokens in a response |\n\n### Connection Lifecycle\n\nThe realtime client manages a connection lifecycle with these statuses:\n\n| Status | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `idle` | Not connected |\n| `connecting` | Establishing connection |\n| `connected` | Active session |\n| `reconnecting` | Reconnecting after interruption |\n| `error` | Connection error occurred |\n\nAnd these modes while connected:\n\n| Mode | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `idle` | Connected but not actively interacting |\n| `listening` | Capturing user audio input |\n| `thinking` | Processing user input |\n| `speaking` | AI is generating a response |\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\nimport { useEffect } from 'react'\n\nconst { status, mode, error, connect, disconnect } = useRealtimeChat({ getToken, adapter: openaiRealtime() })\n\n// Handle connection\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (status === 'error' && error) {\n    console.error('Connection error:', error.message)\n  }\n}, [status, error])\n```\n\n### Message Structure\n\nRealtime messages use a `parts`-based structure similar to `UIMessage`:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { RealtimeMessagePart } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\ninterface RealtimeMessage {\n  id: string\n  role: 'user' | 'assistant'\n  timestamp: number\n  parts: Array<RealtimeMessagePart>\n  interrupted?: boolean\n}\n```\n\nEach part can be one of:\n\n| Part Type | Fields | Description |\n|-----------|--------|-------------|\n| `text` | `content` | Text content from `sendText()` |\n| `audio` | `transcript`, `durationMs` | Transcribed voice content |\n| `tool-call` | `id`, `name`, `arguments`, `input`, `output` | Tool invocation |\n| `tool-result` | `toolCallId`, `content` | Tool execution result |\n| `image` | `data`, `mimeType` | Image sent via `sendImage()` |\n\n### Error Handling\n\nHandle errors through the `onError` callback or the `error` state:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useRealtimeChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { openaiRealtime } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { getToken } from './token'\n\nconst { error } = useRealtimeChat({\n  getToken,\n  adapter: openaiRealtime(),\n  onError: (err: Error) => {\n    if (err.message.includes('Permission denied')) {\n      alert('Microphone access is required for voice chat.')\n    } else {\n      console.error('Realtime error:', err)\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Best Practices\n\n1. **Token security** - Always generate tokens server-side. Never expose API keys to the client.\n2. **Microphone permissions** - Handle the case where the user denies microphone access gracefully.\n3. **Cleanup** - Always disconnect when unmounting components. The `useRealtimeChat` hook handles this automatically.\n4. **Instructions** - Keep voice assistant instructions concise. Remind the model it's in a voice interface so responses stay conversational.\n5. **Tool design** - Keep tool descriptions clear and tool outputs small, since results are processed in real time.\n6. **Error recovery** - Implement retry logic for transient connection failures.\n"}
